5. MODULAR APPLICATION ENTRY POINT (`main.py`) & CORS MIDDLEWARE
================================================================================
Instead of stuffing 20+ endpoints into a single massive file, Zaika organizes endpoints into clean files inside `backend/routers/` and mounts them inside `main.py`.

`CORSMiddleware` is mandatory so your Streamlit frontend (running on port `8501`) is allowed to talk to your FastAPI backend (running on port `8000`).

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI
from fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware
from backend.routers import menu_router

app = FastAPI(
    title="Zaika Restaurant Management API",
    description="Backend REST API for QR Ordering, Staff Floor Map, KDS & Owner Analytics",
    version="1.0.0"
)

# Allow Streamlit frontend to communicate with FastAPI
app.add_middleware(
    CORSMiddleware,
    allow_origins=["*"],  # In production, restrict to your Streamlit domain
    allow_credentials=True,
    allow_methods=["*"],
    allow_headers=["*"],
)

# Register modular routers
app.include_router(menu_router.router)

@app.get("/", tags=["Health"])
def health_check():
    return {"status": "online", "service": "Zaika Restaurant API"}
```

